)*  | USD Coin (USDC)**  | Venice Token (VVV)  | Virtuals Protocol  (VIRTUAL)  | Worldcoin (WLD)*  | World Liberty Financial  (WLFI)*  | XDC Network (XDC)*  | XRP (XRP)\nL267: Zcash (ZEC)  | Zora  (ZORA)*  | 0x Protocol (ZRX)  |  |  |  |  |\nL268: (1) Not all cryptocurrencies are available in every state. An asterisk indicates a cryptocurrency is not currently available for trading in New York; a double asterisk indicates a cryptocurrency is not currently available for trading in New York or Texas.\nL269: \nL270: 6\nL271: \nL272: * * *\nL273: \nL274: 【35†Table of Contents】\nL275: \nL276: CAUTIONARY NOTE REGARDING FORWARD‑LOOKING STATEMENTS\nL277: This Quarterly Report on Form 10-Q (this “Quarterly Report”) of Robinhood Markets, Inc. (“RHM” and, together with its subsidiaries, “we,” “us,” “Robinhood,” or the “Company”) contains forward-looking statements (as such phrase is used in the federal securities laws), which involve substantial risks and uncertainties. Forward-looking statements generally relate to future events or our future financial or operating performance.\nL278: In some cases, you can identify forward-looking statements because they contain words such as “believe,” “may,” “will,” “should,” “expect,” “plan,” “anticipate,” “could,” “intend,” “target,” “project,” “contemplate,” “estimate,” “predict,” “potential,” or “continue,” or the negative of these words or other similar terms or expressions that concern our expectations, strategy, plans or intentions. This Quarterly Report includes, among others, forward-looking statements regarding:\nL279: •our expectations regarding existing and potential future legal and regulatory proceedings, rulemakings, and investigations;\nL280: \nL281: •our intent to continue expanding our operations outside of the United States;\nL282: \nL283: •that we are continuously introducing new products and diversifying our services that further expand access to the financial system;\nL284: \nL285: •our expectations regarding legislative developments and their impact on us, including with respect to the CLARITY Act and the GENIUS Act;\nL286: •our expectation that management will exclude WonderFi from its assessment of internal control over financial reporting for 2026;\nL287: \nL288: •our expectations about adapting our product and service offerings to reflect local regulatory requirements, customer preferences, and other location-specific factors when pursuing such expansion;\nL289: \nL290: •the Repurchase Program and our current expectations with respect to timing;\nL291: •that we expect that Robinhood Chain's underlying protocol will need to be upgraded from time to time to remediate newly discovered vulnerabilities, improve network performance, add new functionality, or comply with evolving regulatory requirements;\nL292: \nL293: •our belief that, based on our current level of operations, our primary sources of liquidity will be adequate to meet our current liquidity needs for the next 12 months;\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nhood-20260930 (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1783879/000178387926000167/hood-20260930.htm)\nciteturn20view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn16view0\",\"lineno\":490}); Total lines: 4228\nL462: Weighted-average shares used to compute net income per share attributable to Robinhood common stockholders:  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL463: Basic  | 889   |  |  | 898   |  |  | 885   |  |  | 899   |\nL464: Diluted  | 918   |  |  | 911   |  |  | 919   |  |  | 913   |\nL465: See Accompanying Notes to the Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements.\nL466: \nL467: 12\nL468: \nL469: * * *\nL470: \nL471: 【35†Table of Contents】\nL472: \nL473: ROBINHOOD MARKETS, INC.\nL474: \nL475: CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF COMPREHENSIVE INCOME\nL476: \nL477: (Unaudited)\nL478:  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL479:  | Three Months 